[1] linearized-GR exchange for conserved sources, p = (w, 0, 0, k) in the CMB frame, eta = diag(-1,1,1,1), units 16 pi G = 1
    200 random conserved pairs: max |p_mu T^mu nu| = 9.6e-15; max rel |E_Lorenz - (TT/s + V/k^2 + S-block)| = 3.2e-15
    E = TT:TT'/(k^2-w^2) - 2 T^0a T'^0a/k^2 + (1/2) rho rho' (k^2-w^2)/k^4 + (1/2)(rho T'_perp + T_perp rho')/k^2  [x 16 pi G]
    => only TT carries the cone pole; V and S blocks are instantaneous (polynomial in w over k^n); S block det = -1/(4k^4) < 0 (indefinite)
    at w -> k: S block entries (1.0e-09, 0.50), V entry -2.00: finite (no 1/s)

    repaired gain f(t) = e^-x x^2 (4-x)/(2 tau): int f = 1.000000000000, first moment = 0.0e+00, third moment = -120.0000 tau^3; f(0) = 0.0, f'(0) = 0.0, f''(0) = 4.0/tau^3

[2] conserved S/V record noise with a finite start t0 = 0 (one mode, k = 2/tau): free data rho, T^0a filtered by the gain; derived
    J^z0 = (i/k) d_t J^00, J^zz = (i/k)^2 d_t^2 J^00  (exact conservation  d_t J^0nu + i k J^z nu = 0)
    repaired n=4: J^0nu(t0) = (-1.6e-17, 0.0e+00); rel. residual nu=0: 1.3e-04; Var J^zz (sample) = 1.679e-01 vs int (f'')^2/k^4 = 1.592e-01
    literal n=2 (f'(0)=1): J^0nu(t0) = (-1.6e-17, 1.9e-03); rel. residual nu=0: 4.6e-02; Var J^zz (sample) = 3.142e+01 vs int (f'')^2/k^4 = 7.838e-02 (white-noise term f'(0) xi present: Var J^zz = infinity in the dt -> 0 limit)
    TT channel: xi^TT_ij is spatial, transverse, traceless => d_mu xi^mu nu = 0 identically, no time derivative, enters no constraint
    => with f(0) = f'(0) = 0 (repaired n = 4; literal n >= 3) the conserved S/V noise starts at zero (J^0nu(t0) = 0, so the Gauss/momentum
       constraints hold with h = hdot = 0 at t0) and every component has finite variance. subtraction: none

[3] mean field with a finite start: J = f *_{t0} T for pre-existing conserved matter (one mode, k = 2, tau = 1)
    repaired n=4: max|defect nu=0| = 0.915 (predicted f(t-t0) T^00(t0): 0.915; max|defect - prediction| = 5.5e-04); nu=z: 0.065 vs 0.065
        with the initial-memory term B: max|defect| = 3.6e-04; J^00(t0+) + B^00(t0) = 1.4551 vs T^00(t0) = 1.4553; Psi1(inf) = 7.23e-13 tau (first moment)
    literal n=3: max|defect nu=0| = 0.394 (predicted f(t-t0) T^00(t0): 0.394; max|defect - prediction| = 1.8e-04); nu=z: 0.028 vs 0.028
        with the initial-memory term B: max|defect| = 1.5e-04; J^00(t0+) + B^00(t0) = 1.4551 vs T^00(t0) = 1.4553; Psi1(inf) = 3.00e+00 tau (first moment)
    B^00 = psi(t-t0) T^00(t0) - Psi1(t-t0) div T^0i(t0),  B^0i = psi(t-t0) T^0i(t0),  B^ij = 0;  psi(s) = int_s^inf f,  Psi1(s) = int_0^s psi
    => R13-6's H3 (h = hdot = 0, couplings switched on) violates the Bianchi identity for t - t0 ~ tau whenever T^0nu(t0) != 0;
       B repairs it exactly and is transient iff the first moment vanishes (repaired gain); the literal gain leaves a frozen B^00 = n tau dT^00/dt(t0)

[4] TT channel: least-decoherence per polarization, S_h,lambda = 8 pi G hbar |F|^2 /(c^2 |W^2 - w^2|) (W = ck); h_lambda = sqrt(8 pi G hbar/c^2) (f * J0(W.)) * xi
    W tau = 0.1: K(0) = 3.6e-17, K'(0) = -4.4e-18; T=30: Var h = 2.2109, Var hdot = 1.4064; T=300: Var h = 3.0233, Var hdot = 2.2292; T=3000: Var h = 3.8398, Var hdot = 3.0469
        slopes per ln T: Var h 0.3546, Var hdot 0.3551; predicted |F(W)|^2/pi = 0.3548
    W tau = 1.0: K(0) = 4.9e-18, K'(0) = -1.4e-17; T=30: Var h = 1.9505, Var hdot = 1.6061; T=300: Var h = 2.7530, Var hdot = 2.3982; T=3000: Var h = 3.5340, Var hdot = 3.1783
        slopes per ln T: Var h 0.3392, Var hdot 0.3388; predicted |F(W)|^2/pi = 0.3382
    int_0^X J0^2 = (ln X + 2.6567)/pi  (ln 8 + gamma_E = 2.6567);  int_0^X J1^2 = (ln X + 0.6567)/pi  (X = 1e5)
    unfiltered kernel J0 (F = 1): hdot = xi - W (J1 * xi), Var hdot = infinity (referee R13-6 point 4); with the gain K(0) = K'(0) = 0 => finite
    energy: rho_GW = (c^2/32 pi G) <hdot_ij hdot_ij>, h_ij = sum_lambda h_lambda e^lambda_ij, e:e = 2, two polarizations
      => rho_GW = (hbar c /(2 pi^3)) int dk k^3 eps |F|^2 [ln(c k t) + c1]  vs R11-5/R13-6 formula (2 hbar c/pi^3) int dk k^3 eps |F|^2 ln(c k t)
      => exact TT weight = 1/4 of the assumed O(1) normalization at leading log; constant c1 = ln 8 + gamma_E - 2 inside the log

[5] CP in the exact limit: approximant kernels J0_N(t) = (1/N) sum_j cos(W cos th_j t) e^{-Gam t} (Gauss-Chebyshev for the arcsine measure)
    ||A||_HS = 2.128e+01 (so ||C||_1 = ||A||_HS^2 = 4.527e+02); quadrature is exact-in-practice for t < ~N/W, so convergence sets in at N ~ T W
    N=   8: ||A_N - A||_HS = 5.25e+01; relative trace-norm bound ||C_N - C||_1/||C||_1 <= 9.09e+00; min Re H_N(Re p >= 0) = 2.44e-03 (positive-real => outer)
    N=  32: ||A_N - A||_HS = 2.09e+01; relative trace-norm bound ||C_N - C||_1/||C||_1 <= 2.36e+00; min Re H_N(Re p >= 0) = 1.59e-05 (positive-real => outer)
    N= 128: ||A_N - A||_HS = 2.58e-02; relative trace-norm bound ||C_N - C||_1/||C||_1 <= 2.43e-03; min Re H_N(Re p >= 0) = 1.59e-03 (positive-real => outer)
    N= 512: ||A_N - A||_HS = 6.47e-03; relative trace-norm bound ||C_N - C||_1/||C||_1 <= 6.08e-04; min Re H_N(Re p >= 0) = 7.15e-04 (positive-real => outer)
    N=2048: ||A_N - A||_HS = 1.62e-03; relative trace-norm bound ||C_N - C||_1/||C||_1 <= 1.52e-04; min Re H_N(Re p >= 0) = 1.84e-04 (positive-real => outer)
    => C_N = A_N A_N^* -> C in trace norm on L^2[t0, t]; Gaussian CP maps with converging covariances converge pointwise; limits of CP maps are CP

